@startuml 08_ai_scoring_formula_comparison
title AI Scoring Formula — Current Bugs vs. Proposed Fixes

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam roundcorner 8

participant "AiWeightedMatchingStrategy\n[CURRENT]" as Current
participant "AiWeightedMatchingStrategy\n[PROPOSED]" as Proposed
participant "MatchingPreference\n[CURRENT normalize()]" as PrefCurrent
participant "MatchingPreference\n[PROPOSED normalize()]" as PrefProposed

note over Current, PrefProposed
    This diagram compares the scoring formula and weight normalization
    for the CURRENT implementation vs. PROPOSED fixes.
    All changes are in Phase 1 (no DB migration required).
end note

== S_trust: Trust Score Clamping (Task 1.1) ==

note over Current #FFE0E0
    CURRENT — scoreTrust():
    S_trust = candidateTrustScore / 10.0

    trustScore=500  → S_trust=50.0  ✓
    trustScore=1000 → S_trust=100.0 ✓
    trustScore=1200 → S_trust=120.0 ✗ EXCEEDS [0,100]

    Result: S_trust > 100 breaks MAX_WEIGHT_CAP=0.70
    A trust-heavy user can exceed their capped weight mathematically.
end note

note over Proposed #E8F5E9
    PROPOSED — scoreTrust():
    S_trust = Math.min(candidateTrustScore / 10.0, 100.0)

    trustScore=500  → S_trust=50.0  ✓
    trustScore=1000 → S_trust=100.0 ✓
    trustScore=1200 → S_trust=100.0 ✓ clamped

    All score components guaranteed in [0, 100].
    MAX_WEIGHT_CAP=0.70 is now mathematically sound.
end note

== S_time: Time Overlap Scoring (Task 1.2) ==

note over Current #FFE0E0
    CURRENT — scoreTime():
    S_time = min(overlapMinutes / 60.0 × 100, 100.0)

    Example: User wants 3h walk (180 min intent duration)
    Candidate A overlaps 60 min  → S_time = 100.0
    Candidate B overlaps 180 min → S_time = 100.0

    Result: A 1-hour overlap and a perfect 3-hour overlap
    score identically. Long-walk users get incorrect matching.
end note

note over Proposed #E8F5E9
    PROPOSED — scoreTime(WalkIntent a, WalkIntent b, ...):
    desiredDuration = min(a.duration, b.duration)
    S_time = min(overlapMinutes / desiredDuration × 100, 100.0)

    Example: User wants 3h walk (180 min intent duration)
    Candidate A (1h intent): desiredDuration=60 min, overlap=60 → S_time=100.0
    Candidate B (3h intent): desiredDuration=180 min, overlap=60 → S_time=33.3
    Candidate C (3h intent): desiredDuration=180 min, overlap=180 → S_time=100.0

    Result: Candidate A (short walk) scores 100 against a 1h-intent user.
    Candidate C (perfect 3h match) scores 100 against a 3h-intent user.
    Differentiation is now accurate.
end note

== S_tags: Empty Profile Score (Task 1.3) ==

note over Current #FFE0E0
    CURRENT — scoreTags():
    if (both tags empty) return 50.0   ← ARTIFICIAL BONUS

    Two new users with no tags get S_tags=50.0
    vs. two users with different tags getting S_tags=0–30.
    Empty profiles are rewarded over real (low-overlap) profiles.
end note

note over Proposed #E8F5E9
    PROPOSED — scoreTags():
    if (both tags empty) return 20.0   ← reduced, not zero (new user tolerance)
    if (one side empty)  return 10.0   ← minimal base signal
    else: Jaccard(tagsA, tagsB) × 100

    New users can still match, but incomplete profiles
    are no longer advantaged over tagged users.
    Encourages profile completion.
end note

== MatchingPreference: Weight Normalization (Task 1.4) ==

note over PrefCurrent #FFE0E0
    CURRENT — normalize():
    Pass 1: divide each weight by sum → sum=1.0
    Pass 2: cap any weight at MAX_WEIGHT_CAP=0.70

    Problem: weightTimeOverlap is NEVER incremented.
    Only weightInterest and weightBehavior are ever bumped.
    After 20+ reviews with INTEREST tags:

    weightInterest   → 0.70 (capped)
    weightBehavior   → 0.18
    weightTimeOverlap → 0.12 → ...→ near 0

    Result: The matching engine forgets that time
    scheduling is important for a walking appointment app.
end note

note over PrefProposed #E8F5E9
    PROPOSED — normalize() with Pass 3:
    Pass 1: divide each weight by sum → sum=1.0
    Pass 2: cap any weight at MAX_WEIGHT_CAP=0.70
    Pass 3: if weightTimeOverlap < MIN_TIME_WEIGHT=0.25:
              floor to 0.25, redistribute deficit
              proportionally from interest+behavior

    After 20+ reviews with INTEREST tags:
    weightInterest    → 0.56 (reduced to give time its floor)
    weightBehavior    → 0.19
    weightTimeOverlap → 0.25 (guaranteed minimum)

    Time scheduling always contributes ≥25% to match scoring.
end note

== Combined Effect on TotalScore ==

note over Current, PrefProposed
    TotalScore = W_time × S_time + W_interest × S_tags + W_behavior × S_trust

    CURRENT example (active user, many INTEREST reviews, high-trust candidate):
    W_time=0.05  × S_time=100 = 5.0
    W_interest=0.65 × S_tags=40  = 26.0
    W_behavior=0.30 × S_trust=120 = 36.0  ← EXCEEDS 100 cap
    TotalScore = 67.0  [distorted — trust dominates, time ignored]

    PROPOSED example (same scenario, all fixes applied):
    W_time=0.25  × S_time=33.3 = 8.3   ← ratio-based
    W_interest=0.55 × S_tags=40  = 22.0
    W_behavior=0.20 × S_trust=100 = 20.0 ← clamped
    TotalScore = 50.3  [accurate — time overlap now differentiates candidates]
end note

@enduml
